The limitation is immediate. A person can raise $w$, but $h$ is bounded: $h \leq h_{\max}
\qquad\Longrightarrow\qquad
I_{\mathrm{labor}} \leq w h_{\max}.$ This is a simple model, but it captures TJ’s claim. If the mechanism is direct labor, income remains tied to the body and calendar of the worker.

