TJ’s example is a business that cash flows at $\$20{,}000$ per month. He then imagines debt service of either $\$7{,}000$ or $\$10{,}000$ per month: $C_{\mathrm{monthly}}=\$20{,}000,
\qquad
D_{\mathrm{monthly}}\in\{\$7{,}000,\ \$10{,}000\}.$ The resulting surplus range is $\begin{aligned}
S_{\mathrm{monthly}}
  &= \$20{,}000-D_{\mathrm{monthly}},\\
  &\in \{\$13{,}000,\ \$10{,}000\}.\end{aligned}$ The clean case in his spoken example is $\$20{,}000-\$10{,}000=\$10{,}000.$

