The same logic appears in the discussion of faith. TJ tells a personal story about belief, then generalizes it: when someone truly believes something, it drives action, thought, and relationships. We can preserve the structure without pretending it is a proof: $\text{belief}
\longrightarrow
\text{action}
\longrightarrow
\text{relationships}
\longrightarrow
\text{opportunity}.$

